@references

Purpose:
  Reusable engineering knowledge. AI loads these once and references
  them across projects instead of re-deriving concepts.

Use this index before introducing any conceptual approach.

Owns: references\index.sdd

Registry:
  Each reference is a trust-weighted knowledge entry. Every entry MUST
  carry the following metadata fields:

  Fields:
    id:               @<namespace>.<name>
    purpose:          one-line description of the rule/practice
    status:           observed | candidate | validated | established | deprecated | unknown
    trust:            low | medium | high | established
    confidence:       low | medium | high
    evidence_count:   integer (total evidence sources)
    by_type:
      code:          integer
      tests:         integer
      tasks:         integer
      decisions:     integer
      projects:      integer
      production:    integer
      external:      integer
      human:         integer
    provenance:       discovered_from / source / extracted_by / validated_by / validated_at
    overrides:        optional list of @reference.id this supersedes in a project
    override_reason:  optional justification for the override

  Example:
    @skill.idempotent-command
      purpose: Prevent duplicate command execution.
      status: validated
      trust: medium
      confidence: high
      evidence_count: 4
      by_type:
        code: 0
        tests: 1
        tasks: 2
        decisions: 0
        projects: 1
        production: 0
        external: 0
        human: 0
      provenance:
        discovered_from: @tmp.payment-service
        source: payment-service repository
        extracted_by: AI
        validated_by: @task.1044
        validated_at: 2026-08-31

Navigation:
  DDD: @ddd
  Architecture: @architecture
  Patterns: @patterns
  Database: @database
  Engineering: @engineering
  BestPractices: @sdd/best-practices.sdd
  SDDTools: @sdd/tool-comparison.sdd
  EARSNotation: @sdd/ears-notation.sdd

DecisionGuide:
  Need domain modeling?
    → @ddd

  Need system structure?
    → @architecture

  Need reusable solution?
    → @patterns

  Need data management?
    → @database

  Need engineering principles?
    → @engineering

  Need default heuristics?
    → @best-practices

  Need to resolve a conflict?
    Apply the priority hierarchy below, then fall back to a
    project-specific decision.

PriorityHierarchy:
  1. Explicit project constraint       (highest — always wins)
  2. Approved project decision
  3. Validated project skill
  4. Established organization knowledge
  5. General best practice
  6. AI suggestion                     (lowest)

  Rule: Generic best practice MUST NOT override a project-specific
  decision. Project-local context always wins over global defaults.

Applicability:
  CoreBanking:
    ddd: STRONG
    architecture: STRONG
    patterns: MEDIUM
    database: STRONG

  Payment:
    ddd: STRONG
    architecture: STRONG
    patterns: STRONG
    database: STRONG

  OrderManagement:
    ddd: STRONG
    architecture: MEDIUM
    patterns: MEDIUM
    database: MEDIUM

  SimpleCRUD:
    ddd: LOW
    architecture: LOW
    patterns: LOW
    database: LOW

  LandingPage:
    ddd: NONE
    architecture: NONE
    patterns: NONE
    database: NONE

State: +

# Reference Intelligence Engine (RIE)

Engine: @engine.sdd (pipeline, contract, matrix, fit, evidence,
freshness — read first)
Web references: @web/ (one REF-<n>.sdd per analyzed reference)
Design: @design/patterns.sdd (distilled patterns), @design/decisions.sdd

Rules:
  [REF-01] References feed decisions; never clone assets/code/markup.
  [REF-02] Intent must be recorded before analysis (default INSPIRE).
  [REF-03] Every adopted pattern carries source REF + reason.
  [REF-04] Reference never overrides project rules ([R110]).
  [REF-05] Research cases are re-runnable (DR-<n> reuse; staleness
           triggers re-analysis on demand).
State: +
